{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark hark fair traveler bound for lands afar\nThy quill doth seek in verse most grand and fair\nAn itinerary knit with thread of time\nWhere cherry blossoms dance and koi do climb\n\n**Day the First Anno Domini of Thy Japanese Flight**\nAwake ere dawn doth break in Tokyo’s light\nTo Asakusa’s temple where lanterns burn bright\nWalk the streets where merchants long have trod\nSavor sweet mochi with matcha’s steadfast God\nAt noon do partake of ramen rich and deep\nThen to Akihabara where dreams and tech do leap\nNeon bright and games that call thy name\nYet heed thy hours lest night doth claim thee lame\n\n**Day the Second Where Shinkansen Doth Gleam**\nBoard the bullet swift on steel that cuts through air\nTo Kyoto fair where temples stand with grace and care\nFushimi Inari’s torii path so red and high\nClimb till zenith where gods do watch the sky\nAt dusk doth Gion’s lanterns softly glow\nGeisha whispers where no words dare show\nSup with kaiseki where season’s touch is spun\nThen rest thy bones ‘neath futon soft and sun\n\n**Day the Third Where Nature’s Majesty Doth Rise**\nTo Nara go where deer with bells do prance\nFeed the gentle souls with crackers in thy hand\nThen to Todai-ji where Buddha’s might doth stand\nA colossus of faith both wise and grand\nTo Osaka’s castle with moat so wide and deep\nWhere history’s breath doth call thee to keep\nAt evening’s fall to Dotonbori’s glow\nTakoyaki hot with fire shall make thy heart aglow\n\n**Day the Fourth Where Countryside Beckons Bold**\nTo Koyasan where monks in silence tread\nHike to Okunoin where spirits softly tread\nStay at temple lodge where incense fills the air\nAnd dreams of enlightenment without a care\nNext to Takayama where old-world charm doth stay\nSanmachi Suji’s lanes where time doth not decay\nSake warm from barrels where brewers toil all day\n\n**Day the Fifth Where Nature’s Splendor Calls Once More**\nTo Hiroshima where peace doth stand forevermore\nAt Miyajima’s torii where tides do kiss the shore\nMomiji manju sweet upon thy tongue doth rest\nThen to Miyajima’s forest where deer and mist do bless\nIn Hiroshima’s park where souls do quietly repose\nLight a paper crane with memories and woes\n\n**Day the Sixth Where Tokyo Once More Doth Lure**\nReturn to neon where futuristic dreams insure\nTo Shibuya’s scramble where strangers intertwine\nStarbucks’ queue where salarymen in haste do dine\nThen to Odaiba where rainbows bridge the bay\nTeamLab Planets where digital realms hold sway\nWalk through light that paints the walls in hues array\n\n**Day the Seventh Where Farewell Must Be Said**\nTo Tsukiji’s market where fish still leap and play\nSushi fresh as dawn where chefs with knives do sway\nLast stroll through Shinjuku where alleyways conceal\nA thousand secrets best left unsung and real\nAt Narita’s gate where flights to distant lands do call\nTake heed fair traveler of this tale so small\n\nThus ends thy sojourn where east and west do meet\nA tapestry of culture time cannot beat\nGo forth with heart both light and spirits high\nFor Japan’s embrace shall stay within thy eye.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.003225721186026931}, {"token": " h", "logprob": -1.8344011306762695}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0036219253670424223}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -2.5159027576446533}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.4300977885723114}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0005372511222958565}, {"token": " bound", "logprob": -0.43545401096343994}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.023687586188316345}, {"token": " lands", "logprob": -1.6556212902069092}, {"token": " af", "logprob": -1.568533182144165}, {"token": "ar", "logprob": -0.0006778326351195574}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.1254485696554184}, {"token": "Th", "logprob": -3.7286813259124756}, {"token": "y", "logprob": -0.2437222